      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 817935767,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "In general I don't like the `Save` button in the Decode As dialog, because I almost always click Ok and expect it to be saved.\n\nThis is the commit message from a change request I made earlier (which @pquantin did not like), and this has some interesting observations I made. I remember we had a discussion, but I don't remember the details (and the old rejected pull request is gone). I think we talked about making Ok doing save, and make a different button to temporarily apply the changes.\n\n```\nDate:   Sat Sep 1 14:16:14 2018 +0200\n\n    Qt: Remove the Save button from DecodeAsDialog\n    \n    This is the only dialog using a Save button for preferences. This will\n    make some user confusions when restart Wireshark or change profile,\n    and the settings are not stored.\n    \n    The decode-as entries will be stored anyway if visiting the preferences\n    dialog or when editing a single preference using the PreferenceEditorFrame\n    so it's not that temporarily as the documentation states.\n    \n    BTW, the user documentation for Decode-As needs an update.\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 4753670,
            "username": "stigbjorlykke",
            "public_email": "",
