      "title": "Enabled Protos dialog: add Save button",
      "message": "Enabled Protos dialog: add Save button\n\nAdd a Save button to the Enabled Protocols dialog. It acts like the\nOK button does on master: it updates the list of enabled/disabled\nprotocols in the user's profile as written on disk.\n\nIn contrast, the OK button still accepts enabled/disabled protocol\nchanges for the current session, but does not write them to disk.\n\nThis behaviour now matches that of the Decode As dialog.\n\nDone as a thought experiment in response to discussion on !5964.\n\nNote: The idea of temporarily enabling/disabling dissectors is not new\nwith this patch. The `--enable-protocol/--disable-protocol` command-line\noptions to Wireshark also cause temporary changes to the\nenabled/disabled status of dissectors which don't get written to disk.\n",
      "author_name": "David Perry",
